as the temperatures warm up out there  one woman is making sure infants and  children are comfortable in the water  with life-saving skills to prevent  drowning her work has inspired many  families including one who knows  firsthand how quickly a tragedy can  occur victoria saha joins us with a look  at how crucial it is to start infant  swimming resource lessons victoria sasha  here in las vegas many homes have pools  which means the dangers of the water  linger on all year long but infants and  small children may not know just how  dangerous it can be which is why it's so  important to teach them how to save  themselves if they go under  many parents think swim lessons are all  a child could ever need to save  themselves in the water we're not going  to teach them how to blow bubbles we're  going to teach them how to hold their  breath but infant swimming resource  lessons also known as isr instructor  jessica tuck says this is a crucial step  that needs to be taken first any kiddo  that could crawl could reach the water  unattended kids are curious they're  competent good job  tucker teaches children how to save  themselves with breathing exercises and  instant reflexes like rolling onto your  back to float up  life-saving scale sierra mendoza says  she wishes she knew of when her son died  after he was pulled from a home pool  during a family gathering by the time we  were ready to leave  he was nowhere to be found an adult had  taken her 17 month old son austin by the  backyard pool  as the adults got distracted austin  stepped onto the pool cover and fell in  and they found him probably about  four feet in  the water just  lifeless austin survived but had severe  neurological damage at only 10 years old  he passed away they have no idea how to  save themselves so they take a breath  and immediately they aspirate mendoza  says it was hard for her to go near a  pool again but eventually learned about  isr she had her youngest go through the  program and is now getting certified to  help other families drowning time  doesn't happen during swimming time and  so we  in isr are setting our kids up for  success we want them to experience  falling into the pool  mendoza has one more week to finish for  her certification and on may 16 she'll  be conducting her first lesson exactly  eight years since austin died if you are  looking to get an instructor for your  child make sure they're certified we  will have more information up on our  website at eight newsnow dot com sasha
 

